From fd139e1287978ae3e7a44f46771f10225f8df045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Uthe <chris.uthe@openhomefoundation.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:02:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional frame observer to the server for protocol
 tracing

SendspinServer takes a frame_observer that is called with every frame each
encrypted connection sends or receives: the cleartext client/init,
server/init, noise/handshake and server/error exchange, then every message
on the Noise transport as plaintext, with inbound messages reassembled from
their fragments. A frame that fails to decrypt or decode is still reported,
as received and with the reason.

Each ObservedFrame carries its direction, phase, data, the server clock time,
a per-server connection number, and the client id once the handshake names
it. Without an observer nothing changes. An observer that raises is logged
once per connection and never affects it.
